{
  "case_id": "2010-08-1448",
  "document_hash": "99131cf9c772150af606e7312e404362fd09c272458ac77ce22316560bea44eb",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Supreme Court",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1448",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "99131cf9c772150af606e7312e404362fd09c272458ac77ce22316560bea44eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-99131cf9c772-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:04 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Zackery P. Morazzini",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1448",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "99131cf9c772150af606e7312e404362fd09c272458ac77ce22316560bea44eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-99131cf9c772-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The California law at issue today before this Court differs from the New York law at issue in Ginsberg in only one respect: Where New York was concerned with minors' access to harmful sexual material outside the guidance of a parent, California is no less concerned with a minor's access to the deviant level of violence that is presented in a certain category of video games that can be no less harmful to the development of minors."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1448",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "99131cf9c772150af606e7312e404362fd09c272458ac77ce22316560bea44eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-99131cf9c772-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What's a deviant -- a deviant, violent video game? As opposed to what? A normal violent video game?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1448",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "99131cf9c772150af606e7312e404362fd09c272458ac77ce22316560bea44eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-99131cf9c772-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: That's an interesting concession on your part, that the labeling doesn't have a need separate from the restriction on sale. I would have thought that if you wanted a lesser restriction, that you would have promoted labeling as a reasonable strict scrutiny restriction to permit the control of sale of these materials to minors, but you seem to have given up that argument altogether."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State of California",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1448",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "99131cf9c772150af606e7312e404362fd09c272458ac77ce22316560bea44eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-99131cf9c772-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MORAZZINI: It's important to the State of California that the parent -- that we ensure that the parent can involve themselves in this important decision."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1448",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "99131cf9c772150af606e7312e404362fd09c272458ac77ce22316560bea44eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-99131cf9c772-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: I can see your white light's on. But even if we get past what I think are difficult questions about vagueness and how to interpret this law, isn't there a less restrictive alternative with the -- a V-chip?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Smith",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1448",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "99131cf9c772150af606e7312e404362fd09c272458ac77ce22316560bea44eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-99131cf9c772-0001-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SMITH: They cost in the range of $50 to $60 when new, Your Honor."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents (California)",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1448",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "99131cf9c772150af606e7312e404362fd09c272458ac77ce22316560bea44eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-99131cf9c772-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SMITH: -- is that there is not a violence exception to the First Amendment for minors, and there should not be."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1448",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "99131cf9c772150af606e7312e404362fd09c272458ac77ce22316560bea44eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-99131cf9c772-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Smith, do you think all video games are speech in the first instance? Because you could look at these games and say they're the modern-day equivalent of Monopoly sets. They're games. They're things that people use to compete. You know, when you think about some of them -- the first video game was Pong. It was playing tennis on your TV. How is that speech at all?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1448",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "99131cf9c772150af606e7312e404362fd09c272458ac77ce22316560bea44eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-99131cf9c772-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Well, what -- what about a\nlaw that says you can't sell to minors a video game -\u00ad\nit doesn't care what the plot is, but no video game in\nwhich the minor commits violent acts of maiming,\nkilling, setting people on fire? What about that?\nWould that -- would that be regulating speech?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1448",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "99131cf9c772150af606e7312e404362fd09c272458ac77ce22316560bea44eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-99131cf9c772-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: So that under -\u00ad whether you use the Salerno test or the Glucksberg test, if there is either one or any applications that would satisfy the Constitution, the facial challenge fails. Right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1448",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "99131cf9c772150af606e7312e404362fd09c272458ac77ce22316560bea44eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-99131cf9c772-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Do you think Mortal Kombat is prohibited by this statute?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1448",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "99131cf9c772150af606e7312e404362fd09c272458ac77ce22316560bea44eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-99131cf9c772-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Would a video game that portrayed a Vulcan, as opposed to a human being, being maimed and tortured -- would that be covered by the Act?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. MORAZZINI",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1448",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "99131cf9c772150af606e7312e404362fd09c272458ac77ce22316560bea44eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-99131cf9c772-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm willing to state right here in open court that the video game Postal 2, yes, would be covered by this Act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1448",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "99131cf9c772150af606e7312e404362fd09c272458ac77ce22316560bea44eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-99131cf9c772-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So if the -- if the video producer says this is not a human being, it's an android computer-simulated person, then that doesn't -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1448",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "99131cf9c772150af606e7312e404362fd09c272458ac77ce22316560bea44eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-99131cf9c772-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So what happens when the character gets maimed, head chopped off, and immediately after it happens they spring back to life and they continue their battle? Is that covered by your Act? Because they haven't been maimed and killed forever. Just temporarily."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. MORAZZINI",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1448",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "99131cf9c772150af606e7312e404362fd09c272458ac77ce22316560bea44eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-99131cf9c772-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Under the Act, yes, because California's concern -- I think this is one of the reasons that sex and violence are so similar. These are base physical acts we're talking about, Justice Sotomayor. So limiting, narrowing our law here in California -- there in California -- to violence, violent depictions against human beings -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. MORAZZINI",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1448",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "99131cf9c772150af606e7312e404362fd09c272458ac77ce22316560bea44eb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-99131cf9c772-0003-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I would think so. The intent of the law is to limit minors' access to those games -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1448",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "99131cf9c772150af606e7312e404362fd09c272458ac77ce22316560bea44eb",
